# A go.work is a property of one engineer's checkout, not of the repository. It
# names the sibling clones that make a theme build against the framework from
# source, and a clean clone of this module has no business knowing their paths:
# without the file, `go build` resolves the published version of the theme, which
# is the answer a stranger to this checkout wants. Committing it would replace that
# with "directory not found".
go.work
go.work.sum

# Where `make build` puts compiled binaries. -o dist/ is used rather than the
# default because the example's main package lives in a directory named tasks, and
# a bare build would collide with it.
dist/
